01:53:12.500 --> 01:53:18.180
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: And meron pang ibang international seminars na inattendan mo? International,

01:53:18.400 --> 01:53:18.760
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: sir,

01:53:18.840 --> 01:53:19.080
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: but

01:53:19.080 --> 01:53:19.880
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: it is conducted

01:53:19.880 --> 01:53:20.560
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: locally,

01:53:20.740 --> 01:53:21.620
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: the Interpol, sir.

01:53:22.080 --> 01:53:26.520
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Interpol? Yes, Your Honor. Okay. I have no further questions. Thank you, Senator

01:53:26.520 --> 01:53:26.880
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Judge

01:53:26.880 --> 01:53:27.260
Sen. Francis “Kiko” Pangilinan: Molina.

01:53:27.280 --> 01:53:30.940
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Ontiveros is recognized. You may proceed, ma'am, and you have two minutes.

01:53:34.870 --> 01:53:36.470
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer.

01:53:40.110 --> 01:54:09.980
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Para sa Counsel for the Defense, Mr. Presiding Officer, just for clarity, ano pong relevance nung video na ipinakita ni Atty. Zuleika Lopez? Sinasabi po ba ng depensa na 'yung mga alleged threats o alleged incitements ni VP Duterte ay prompted nung detensyon ni Atty. Lopez?

01:54:11.280 --> 01:55:09.780
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Yes, Your Honor. There was a systematic oppression made by the House of Representatives dating back from their, um, their—even before their mini trial, Your Honor. Their, uh, the committee headed by Representative Joel Chua began investigating the Vice President and her people. Even when Atty. Zuleika Lopez was being interviewed by the House Quad Com Committee, Your Honor, even if she was answering the questions faithfully and to the best of her ability, she was cited in contempt, detained. Her lawyer was not allowed to be with her when they were trying to detain her in the women's correctional facility, Your Honor.

01:55:10.370 --> 01:55:28.630
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: So, Mr. Presiding Officer, counsel for the defense, is the defense in a position to overcome alleged grave threats if there is a legitimate reason to guard?

01:55:32.260 --> 01:55:34.140
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Your Honor, that is not the point.

01:55:34.790 --> 01:56:21.510
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: No, no, no. Mr. Presiding Officer, I am making a point through my question, and I am asking the good counsel for the defense, dahil sinabi nila there was a systematic oppression, that yes, yan po ang nag-prompt nung alleged grave threats and alleged incitements ng Vice President, nag-prompt po ng detensyon ni Atty. Lopez na kanyang inilarawan sa ipinakitang video kanina. So I am asking if that is the position of the defense that it is okay or it is acceptable to accept grave threats if there is a legitimate reason to guard. Yes,

01:56:21.510 --> 01:56:21.810
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Your Honor.

01:56:21.950 --> 01:56:23.410
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Yes, Mr. President.

01:56:27.710 --> 01:56:28.190
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: No,

01:56:28.270 --> 01:56:30.590
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Your Honor. I was just referring to before.

01:56:30.590 --> 01:57:22.450
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We would like to remind the senator judges to be cautious in making counsels for either party. Make conclusions of law and fact. Instead of presenting evidence through a witness, they will present or through direct, cross, redirect, or recross. Because if he answers, Senator Judge Diveros, That would effectively place on record a conclusion of fact and law, not drawn from a witness, which they can very well do so during their closing remarks. And when I allow them to speak by way of repartee to the preparation yesterday and discussion yesterday by counsel for the prosecution. But other than that, as agreed with some of the senator judges, we would try to limit the answers of the counsels for the parties. With your indulgence, Senator Judge Ontiveros, please. I

01:57:22.450 --> 01:58:14.910
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: submit, Mr. Presiding Officer. May I just in closing make of record that I also appreciated and also submitted to the ruling of the Presiding Officer yesterday because I appreciated that it partook of the history of impeachment proceedings in this court. I also carefully studied the past impeachment trials and found that Pati noon, naging liberal ang pagpapahintulot nila sa mga katanungan. Katanungan ng mga senator judges para lang mas maliwanagan ang iba't ibang punto. So I again thank the good presiding officer and again reiterate my submission to his ruling and thank the good counsel for the defense for his response.

01:58:15.070 --> 01:58:23.330
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We thank Senator Antiveros for her indulgence and understanding. Senator Villanueva and thereafter, Senate President Gachalian.

01:58:25.390 --> 01:58:27.630
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

01:58:27.850 --> 01:59:50.230
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Mr. President, Mr. Presiding Officer. May I just point out something to the witness? Mr. President, Your Honors, the witness mentioned yesterday that reported statements of the Vice President were referred to the Presidential Security Command and evaluated in coordination with the National Security Council. Just to assist the court in evaluating the relevance and weight of the government security response in determining whether the respondent's conduct constitutes an impeachable offense, may we know from the witness, could the witness explain how threats against the president are ordinarily assessed? By the government. Kasi o, dito yung lumalabas yung pag-weigh natin whether or not meron bang bigat iyong threat o ito'y ordinaryong threat na nangyayari sa pang-araw-araw nating buhay. Specifically, Mr. Witness, what factors are taken into account in evaluating a reported threat and in determining appropriate measures?

01:59:51.360 --> 01:59:58.610
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Oo. I can't answer on the part of the NSC or DNO because I'm not part of the institution.

02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:01.400
Sen. Joel Villanueva: In your capacity as an agent?

02:00:01.420 --> 02:00:11.560
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: In my capacity, one of the considerations, if it's an active threat, if it's the one giving the threat is capable of doing so.

02:00:12.380 --> 02:00:12.900
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Meaning?

02:00:14.180 --> 02:00:15.260
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: High-ranking

02:00:15.260 --> 02:00:16.360
Sen. Joel Villanueva: officials, and if

02:00:16.360 --> 02:00:17.140
Sen. Joel Villanueva: you say an official?

02:00:17.140 --> 02:00:25.520
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: A capability or power to implement such threat, it is considered, sir.

02:00:25.740 --> 02:00:42.900
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Example, a mayor, perhaps? Would you say a high-ranking official? A congressman? Or yung basihan po ng kanyang threat? Kunyari ang threat ko, dadalhin kita doon sa buwan. Wala naman akong space shuttle. So wala din pong bearing yun. Is that the correct assumption?

02:00:44.780 --> 02:00:57.680
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Not only, sir, but also how it was delivered, sir. Like what was mentioned in the, that I mentioned previously, it was mentioned that no joke, no joke. It's a serious.

02:00:58.420 --> 02:00:59.360
Sen. Joel Villanueva: So that is the

02:00:59.360 --> 02:01:00.220
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: consideration.

02:01:01.600 --> 02:01:12.860
Sen. Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much. And lastly, Mr. Witness, you made mention na submit mo sa DOJ nung January 30. Is it the same affidavit that you submitted to the HOR?

02:01:14.480 --> 02:01:19.000
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: The one that submitted to the HOR is the affidavit dated February, sir.

02:01:19.550 --> 02:01:20.550
Sen. Joel Villanueva: So, that's the latest.

02:01:20.950 --> 02:01:24.230
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yes, sir. The one that complied with the requirements of the DOJ, sir. Thank

02:01:24.230 --> 02:01:27.010
Sen. Joel Villanueva: you very much for that clarification. Thank you, Mr. President. Thank

02:01:27.010 --> 02:01:51.300
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: you, Senator Villanueva. Before I recognize Senate President Gachalian and thereafter, Senator Erwin Tulfo, may I remind Atty. Narvasa that your five minutes, you'll be given your five minutes after the questions of the Senator judges and before we recognize the counsel for the prosecutor for his redirect. Second President, Gachal Yanes, recognized. You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

02:01:51.300 --> 02:01:55.750
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: May I be clarified? I believe that we would do it after re-cross.

02:01:55.750 --> 02:01:58.900
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: I heard cross. After re-cross.

02:01:58.900 --> 02:02:00.470
Atty. Carlo Joaquin T. Narvasa: Yes, Your Honor. Thank you, Your Honor.

02:02:00.530 --> 02:02:01.090
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Better for us?

02:02:01.310 --> 02:02:14.390
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yes, Your Honor. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. I just have a few questions. Clarificatory questions. Narinig ko kanina ginong testigo na nasabi niyo may 40 media personalities doon sa Prescon. Tama po ba?

02:02:14.770 --> 02:02:15.450
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yes, Your Honor.

02:02:15.710 --> 02:02:18.560
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Pero ang inyong inibitahan, Anim lang?

02:02:18.900 --> 02:02:19.820
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yes, Your Honor.

02:02:20.060 --> 02:02:21.600
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Bakit anim lang?

02:02:21.600 --> 02:02:36.060
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: The 40, we see the number of participants but the number of person who ask the vice president during that time, it's limited. And we consider who we sure that is present during that time, Your Honor.

02:02:39.560 --> 02:02:58.920
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Mayroon bang kayong criteria kung paano pipiliin itong? Ang mga media personalities or kung sino lang ang nagtanong? Kasi kahit hindi ka naman magtatanong, nandoon ka naman, naririnig mo yung mga diskusyon, meron ba kayong mga criteria kung paano pumipili ng media personalities?

02:03:00.360 --> 02:03:08.160
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yung sure po namin na present during that time. Kasi kapag hindi po kasi kayo nagtanong, hindi po magpa-pop up yung mukha nyo tsaka yung pangalan nyo.

02:03:09.040 --> 02:03:19.160
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Okay. At... Itong mga anim na sinupinan ninyo, ano yung kanyang common statement na ibinigay?

02:03:19.820 --> 02:03:28.820
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Kinonfirm po nila na present sila during the November 23, 2024 press conference and yung utterance po ni Vice President narinig po nila.

02:03:28.960 --> 02:03:57.650
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Okay, I believe ilan dito sa mga personalities ay ipapatawag rin. So tatalon ako sa ibang topic. Nakita ko kanina itong tungkol sa Atty. Max Corr Interventures At nakita ko kanina, pinakita yung Articles of Incorporation, mukha siyang supplier ng equipment. Ngayon nasabi rin na doon ka nag-training for two weeks. Sino nagbayad nung training?

02:03:58.890 --> 02:04:12.340
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Sir, the training is included in the procurement of digital forensic tools. In the procurement document, ni-require po si MaxCorp na mag-provide po ng training included in the equipment, sir.

02:04:12.340 --> 02:04:13.800
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yung paggamit ng equipment?

02:04:13.800 --> 02:04:17.570
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Tsaka yung ano po, yung process po ng digital forensic as a whole.

02:04:17.950 --> 02:04:43.010
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Yung kanya lang, sila ba ay... Diba sa mga IT, let's say Oracle, alam natin kilala yan pagdating sa IT. Si MaxCore ba ay kilala pagdating sa digital forensic training? Kasi sa alam, nakita ko kanina talagang supplier sila but are they a well-known or internationally renowned training organization?

02:04:45.690 --> 02:04:53.510
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: It is not the MAC score itself, but it's the trainer that they provide, sir, that is capable in training us, sir.

02:04:54.050 --> 02:04:59.290
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Itong trainer na ito, certified siya in this type of technology?

02:04:59.810 --> 02:05:04.550
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yes, sir. The trainer has a lot of certifications in relation to digital forensics, sir.

02:05:04.650 --> 02:05:08.670
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Can you name a few certifications na meron itong trainer na ito?

02:05:09.610 --> 02:05:12.190
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Oo. I can't remember, sir. Let's

02:05:12.190 --> 02:05:15.050
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: say Oracle or let's say Microsoft, di ba? May mga ganyan yan.

02:05:15.050 --> 02:05:27.070
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: No, sir. CompTIA, sir. CompTIA training. I believe he also have a certified ethical hacking certification and a lot more, sir. When it was presented to us, sir.

02:05:27.310 --> 02:05:35.810
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Alright. So, itong mga trainers nito ay certified trainers na pwedeng mag-train sa iyo at magiging certified ka rin.

02:05:36.300 --> 02:05:37.620
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Yes, sir. In-issue na akong certificate.

02:05:37.780 --> 02:05:44.760
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Lastly, Mr. Presiding Officer, after training, nakakuha ka ba ng certification na katulad sa kanila?

02:05:45.600 --> 02:05:49.360
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: No, sir. But that certification that I was trained by them, sir.

02:05:49.680 --> 02:05:59.140
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Pero ikaw mismo, are you certified to do forensic examinations for your purpose and responsibility?

02:05:59.790 --> 02:06:04.910
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: I have a certification, sir. I am a certified computer hacking forensic investigator, sir.

02:06:04.990 --> 02:06:10.150
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Itong forensic analysis, meron kang, for this purpose, itong pinag-uusapan natin.

02:06:10.230 --> 02:06:15.650
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: The computer, the authentication, sir, part, or as a whole, sir?

02:06:15.650 --> 02:06:17.180
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: As a whole, as a whole.

02:06:18.000 --> 02:06:23.600
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: I have a certification in computer hacking, sir. Specific. But I have trainings in relation to the—

02:06:23.600 --> 02:06:32.040
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: Iba yung hacking eh. Yung pinag-uusapan natin forensic examination ng video, forensic examination ng mga ganitong bagay. Meron kang certification doon?

02:06:32.260 --> 02:06:32.820
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: I have

02:06:32.820 --> 02:06:33.460
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: certificate, sir.

02:06:33.680 --> 02:06:35.600
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: All right. Thank you. Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:06:35.860 --> 02:06:39.020
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Erwin Tulfo, thereafter, Senator Judge Marcos.

02:06:40.990 --> 02:06:42.850
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: You may proceed, sir. You have two minutes.

02:06:45.080 --> 02:06:48.640
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair, Mr. Presiding Officer.

02:06:50.470 --> 02:06:52.670
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Ang katanungan ko po ay para sa ating testigo.

02:06:54.790 --> 02:07:20.710
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Batid ko po na sa ilalim ng Republic Act 108-67, sa ilalim po ng Section 4, ang kapangyarihan po ng inyong ahensya na mag-imbestiga kapag na mga krimen particular na tulad ng mga banta sa buhay ng Pangulo, ikalawang Pangulo, Senate President, Speaker of the House, at Chief Justice. Tama po iyon. Yes, Your Honor.

02:07:23.190 --> 02:07:48.090
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Lalo pa at pag ito ay may kaugnayan sa national security, tama po? Yes, Your Honor. Pero ang tanong ko po, ang pagsasampa po ba ng kaso, nasa mandato rin po ba ng NBI na magsampa ng kaso doon sa mga tao na nagbanta sa buhay ng Pangulo, ikalawang Pangulo, Senate President, Speaker of the House, Chief Justice, is it automatic?

02:07:50.780 --> 02:08:10.900
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Or kailangan mag-request sila sa inyo? Matic ba yung pagsasampa ng kaso doon sa nagbanta in this case? Is it automatic or wala lang? Kasama sa mandato niyo to file charges dahil binantaan mo Pangulo o si Vice Presidente kung sino man yung apat na matataas na opisyal natin or limang matataas opisyal natin.

02:08:11.180 --> 02:08:32.010
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: Ang basis namin doon, Your Honor, is the primary objective namin to investigate cases—the threat to the President, Vice President, Senate President, Supreme Court—and if we found that the evidence is enough that there is a crime committed, we will file a case because that's the output of our investigation.

02:08:32.010 --> 02:08:46.670
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: [unclear]

02:08:47.820 --> 02:09:20.990
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Yes, Your Honor. Okay. Hindi niyo na siya kailangan tanungin pa na, sir, gusto niyo po bang kasuhan namin ito? Wala nang ganun. You will never ask. Sabihin natin, hindi lang Pangulo. Vice Presidente. Nangyari din sa Vice Presidente o sa Speaker of the House, sa Senate President o sa Chief Justice. Hindi niyo naman lang siya afford to ask him, like, sir, will you go through the process? Kasi magpa-file ka po ng mga affidavit. This is a long process, etc. Kahit na Pangulo ka po, may pipirmahan ka mga affidavit. Is it automatic, Mr. Witness?

02:09:21.350 --> 02:09:25.970
John Mark Sta. Ana Calilung: We submitted it, sir, even without a complaint for preliminary investigation, sir.

02:09:26.530 --> 02:09:29.030
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: No further questions, Mr. President.

02:09:29.050 --> 02:09:34.770
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Erwin Tulfo. Senator Judge Marcos is recognized. You may proceed, ma'am, and you have two minutes.

02:09:35.240 --> 02:10:13.650
Sen. Imee Marcos: Yes, maraming salamat. Mahal na naman muna. Hihingi lang po ako ng dokumento para mas madali nating sundan ang mga pangyayari. Nalilito lahat pagkat wala po kaming papel. At ang nabigay sa amin, eto, Annex FFFGGG. Nalilito po kami kung alin dito yung mga papel. Kung maaari kaming bigyan, unang-una, yung unang tinutukoy, the first affidavit of investigation dated January 30 alleging grave threats inciting to sedition ng NBI. Ikalawa, yung napasok na yata sa record pero nais rin namin bilang senator-judge na magkaroon ng kopya nung DOJ

02:10:15.230 --> 02:12:04.480
Sen. Imee Marcos: Certification signed by Prosecutor Bandung, February 5, na nagbigay ng 7 grounds na insufficient for preliminary investigation. Ikatlo, yung naibigay na, ito klaro to, naibigay po ni Mavic at ng iba pang staff natin, yung February 10, yung ikalawang amended na ibinigay na revised affidavit of authentication, February 11. Ngunit sabi ni Testigo Calilung na merong kasama ito na wala rito sa record natin at sana maibigay si Sen. Judge. Ito yung sulat kasama nung Second Revised Affidavit of Authentication. Ito naman yung sinasabing sulat ni Santiago Que... Fadulyon ng DOJ na nagsasaad na hindi kailangan na may private complainant yung sina presidente, ang first lady, at saka yung dating speaker dahil base sa kaso ng Santos Concho versus DOJ na 2008 eh hindi daw kailangan yung private complainant. May we also have a copy of the same. Finally, may we urge that a copy also be given of February 14 certification of DOJ asserting that the revised affidavit of investigation was finally sufficient. Nais lang namin makita yun at alamin yung investigation data huling-huli nung March 7, almost a month after the submission of the Affidavit of Authentication kasi halos isang buwan bago utusan na magkaroon ng investigation data form. Sana may kopya rin tayo noon.

02:12:05.500 --> 02:12:08.500
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: To respond to Senator Judge Marcos,

02:12:10.490 --> 02:12:55.920
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: What the court has copies of are the pre-marked documents that the parties pre-marked during pre-trial, but not documents that have not yet been pre-marked. Most of the documents he mentioned that was discussed by counsel for respondent has not yet been pre-marked. They only used it to confront via cross-examination the witness of the prosecution. But the ones we have, We will furnish you with a reminder, of course, Senator Judge Marcos, that these documents have not yet been formally offered by either party and we still have to await formal offer before the court rules on the admissibility, if at all, of these documents. But we will endeavor to furnish the good Senator Judge with whatever the Clerk has.

02:12:56.500 --> 02:13:13.360
Sen. Imee Marcos: Yes, if we could be provided with whatever the clerk has and adequately identified, not as GGGGG or FFFFF. At sana kung mabuo yung mga dokumentong sinasabi sa lalong madaling panahon. Maraming salamat.

02:13:13.500 --> 02:13:22.600
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We will endeavor to comply as best we can, Senator Judge Marcos. Senator Judge Alan Cayetano, what is your pleasure, sir?

02:13:25.930 --> 02:13:35.430
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Sir President and Mr. Presiding Officer, before I ask to be allowed to ask a question, can I just follow up yung kay Sen. Marcos, including the ruling yesterday?

02:13:37.930 --> 02:13:49.790
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Just in the interest of all Sen. Judges being able to follow closely, especially kami sa first row kasi medyo nagkaka-stiff neck na kami. Mahirap tignan yung…

02:13:51.870 --> 02:14:11.230
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Maglalagay na po kami ng TV sa harap ng lanyasan ng Council for Parties. I think all of us own a iPad or a tablet. I don't know what the solution is, but if the Secretariat or the Clerk of Court, the Office of the Clerk of Court can work with our staff.

02:14:15.740 --> 02:14:45.480
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: Just to give you an example for today, if you look at the impeachment complaint, On page 19, for example, it says that the affidavit we're looking for kanina, footnote number 72, is this one. In the impeachment complaint, it's found on Annex G. So this is Annex G.

02:14:48.400 --> 02:14:53.610
